---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SocialLinks from "../components/SocialLinks.astro";

const blog_repo = "https://github.com/jamesyoung-15/jyyoung";
---

<BaseLayout
  pageTitle="About - James Young"
  description="About James Young - platform engineer working on automations and infrastructure as code."
>
  <h1>About</h1>

  <h2>About Me</h2>
  <p class="body-text">
    I'm currently a Platform Engineer working in Boston where I mainly build
    automations for deploying and configuring infrastructure. I grew up and
    studied in Hong Kong before moving to Boston in 2024.
  </p>
  <p class="body-text">
    Outside of work, I enjoy building my homelab (basically my job in a
    non-enterprise environment), building hobby projects, playing videogames,
    and football (soccer).
  </p>
  <p class="body-text">You can find/contact me with the links below.</p>

  <SocialLinks />

  <h2>About My Blogs</h2>
  <p class="body-text">
    My blog posts are just random things I find interesting or wanted to write
    about and are mainly for myself.
  </p>
  <p class="body-text">
    The blog website is built with Astro + CSS with Rose Pine theme (
    <a href={blog_repo} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
      repo link
    </a>
    ). It's currently hosted on Cloudflare Pages although I plan on moving it to
    my homelab later.
  </p>
  <p class="body-text">
    LLM Disclosure: All my blog posts are completely hand-written as I strongly
    dislike the way LLM writes, although the topic itself may be related to LLMs
    in some manner. For example, a project/findings may have been assisted by
    LLM agents along the way. The actual blog post itself will always be
    hand-written by me.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .body-text {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem 0;
    max-width: 75ch;
  }

  .body-text:last-of-type {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .body-text a {
    color: var(--blue);
  }

  .body-text a:hover {
    color: var(--rp-iris);
  }
</style>
